# flash-relay worker-provider configuration example.
#
# Copy to .env in the directory you run flash-relay from, or point
# FLASH_RELAY_ENV at any file. Every line here is commented: no key ships
# in a repo. Process environment variables always win over this file, and
# absent files are the normal zero-config case (a logged-in ZCode install
# needs nothing here).
#
# Precedence for every key: environment > this file > built-in defaults.

# Worker provider: http (default) | openai | claude-cli (experimental).
# http speaks the Anthropic Messages wire format; any Anthropic-compatible
# endpoint needs only the three lines below, no provider value to set.
#FLASH_RELAY_PROVIDER=http

# Endpoint base; the provider appends its own path (/v1/messages for http,
# /chat/completions for openai). Ignored by claude-cli.
#FLASH_RELAY_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic

# Worker model id. Ignored by claude-cli.
#FLASH_RELAY_MODEL=GLM-5.3-Flash

# Worker API key. Falls back to the ZCode stores
# (~/.zcode/cli/config.json, then ~/.zcode/v2/config.json) when unset.
#FLASH_RELAY_API_KEY=

# claude binary for the claude-cli provider (experimental).
#FLASH_RELAY_CLAUDE_BIN=claude

# Explicit config file path (default: ./.env relative to the working
# directory flash-relay runs from).
#FLASH_RELAY_ENV=

# Decision head: vision (default) | jev. The --head flag overrides this
# per run. The jev head needs a TypeSafe key; its keys live in
# ~/.config/flash-relay/jev.env (mode 600), never in a repo tree:
#   TYPESAFE_API_KEY        required when head=jev
#   TYPESAFE_MODEL          default jev-1.13.0, pinned versioned ids only
#   JEV_MIN_CONFIDENCE      default 0.0 (untuned until live data)
#   JEV_MAX_DECISION_AGE_S  default 45
#FLASH_RELAY_HEAD=jev
